{| border=0 cellspacing=2 |- |[[Image:Ife x2critdbswd.gif|right|Devastating critical (bastard sword)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdbaxe.gif|right|Devastating critical (battleaxe)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdclub.gif|right|Devastating critical (club)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdcrea.gif|right|Devastating critical (creature)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critddagg.gif|right|Devastating critical (dagger)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critddart.gif|right|Devastating critical (dart)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critddmac.gif|right|Devastating critical (dire mace)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critddaxe.gif|right|Devastating critical (double axe)]] |[[Image:Ife x2dcrtdwax.gif|right|Devastating critical (dwarven waraxe)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2critdgaxe.gif|right|Devastating critical (greataxe)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdgswd.gif|right|Devastating critical (greatsword)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdhalb.gif|right|Devastating critical (halberd)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdhaxe.gif|right|Devastating critical (handaxe)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdhxb.gif|right|Devastating critical (heavy crossbow)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdhfla.gif|right|Devastating critical (heavy flail)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdkama.gif|right|Devastating critical (kama)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdkatn.gif|right|Devastating critical (katana)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdkukr.gif|right|Devastating critical (kukri)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2critdlxb.gif|right|Devastating critical (light crossbow)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdlfla.gif|right|Devastating critical (light flail)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdlham.gif|right|Devastating critical (light hammer)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdlbow.gif|right|Devastating critical (longbow)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdlswd.gif|right|Devastating critical (longsword)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdmace.gif|right|Devastating critical (mace)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdmsta.gif|right|Devastating critical (morningstar)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdqsta.gif|right|Devastating critical (quarterstaff)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdrapr.gif|right|Devastating critical (rapier)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2critdscim.gif|right|Devastating critical (scimitar)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdscyt.gif|right|Devastating critical (scythe)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdsbow.gif|right|Devastating critical (shortbow)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdsswd.gif|right|Devastating critical (shortsword)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdshur.gif|right|Devastating critical (shuriken)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdskle.gif|right|Devastating critical (sickle)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdslng.gif|right|Devastating critical (sling)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critspr.gif|right|Devastating critical (spear)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdtaxe.gif|right|Devastating critical (throwing axe)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2dcrttri.gif|right|Devastating critical (trident)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdtswd.gif|right|Devastating critical (two-bladed sword)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdunar.gif|right|Devastating critical (unarmed strike)]] |[[Image:Ife x2critdwham.gif|right|Devastating critical (warhammer)]] |[[Image:Ife x2dcrtwhip.gif|right|Devastating critical (whip)]] |} {{feat |epic=yes |type=combat |prereq=[[strength]] 25+, [[cleave]], [[great cleave]], [[improved critical]] (weapon to be chosen), [[overwhelming critical]] (weapon to be chosen), [[power attack]], <del>[[weapon focus]] (weapon to be chosen)</del> |desc=Whenever scoring a [[critical hit]] with the chosen weapon, the character's target must make a [[fortitude]] [[saving throw|save]] or die instantly. Creatures who are immune to critical hits are not affected by this feat. |use=automatic |bonus1=arcane archer |bonus2=barbarian |bonus3=blackguard |bonus4=champion of Torm |bonus5=dwarven defender |bonus6=fighter |bonus7=paladin |bonus8=weapon master }}
==Notes==
*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. *The in-game description lists ''weapon focus'' as a prerequisite, but it is not one. *The [[difficulty class]] of the save is 10 + ½ [[character level]] + [[strength]] [[ability modifier|modifier]]. *Immunity from [[death magic]] does not protect from this feat. *This feat is often banned from online [[persistent world]] [[multiplayer]] servers as some consider it overpowered.

{{feat |type=class |prereq=[[dwarven defender]] 1 |desc=When he needs to, the defender can become a stalwart bastion of defense. In this defensive stance, a defender gains phenomenal strength and durability, but he cannot move from the spot he is defending. He gains the following benefits: * +2 [[strength]] * +4 [[constitution]] * +2 resistance bonus on all [[saving throw|save]]s * +4 [[dodge bonus]] on [[armor class|AC]] At first level, this ability can be used once per day. Every 2 [[class level|level]]s beyond 1, the dwarven defender gains an additional use per day. |use=combat mode |icon=ife_x2defstance.gif |class1=dwarven defender }}
== Notes ==
*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. *This feat does not work with ranged weapons. *The bonuses granted by this feat are subject to the [[ability cap]] of +12, the dodge AC cap of +20, and the saving throw cap of +20. *''Defense stance'' mode automatically drops if the character's current target is removed and all other opponents are out of reach. *A character in a ''defensive stance'' may manually target an out-of-reach opponent, but will not move to engage such an opponent. *An opponent can back out of reach of a character in a ''defensive stance'' or become [[invisible]]. Since the opponent is not removed, this will not cancel the stance. On the other hand, the character will not move to re-engage this opponent. *If a party member comes between a character and his target, the character might drop out of ''defensive stance'' mode, just as when there are no more targets. *The ''defensive stance'' mode will often break (keeping the immobility but losing the bonuses) if the character attempts any action other than attacking. ''(This is likely a bug.)'' * If switched from another combat mode (like [[expertise]]), ''defensive stance'' mode will not add any bonuses but will still consume a daily use. ''(This is likely a bug.)''

{{feat |type=general |prereq=[[base attack bonus]] +2 |desc=The character knows brutal and effective fighting tactics. By sacrificing all other attacks during the [[round]], the character can elect to perform a '''dirty fighting''' move that will deal an extra 1[[d4]] points of damage. This mode cannot be used with [[power attack]]. |use=combat mode |icon=ife_x1dirfig.gif }}
== Notes ==
* Added in the [[expansion pack]]s. * ''Dirty fighting'' can be useful at low levels, but it rapidly loses its net advantage as the character gains more attacks per round. Most players think this feat is nearly useless and should be avoided. * Only normal attacks (including [[off-hand]] attacks) are sacrificed when in this combat mode. Bonus attacks (as from ''[[divine power]]'' or [[cleave]]) are not sacrificed and also receive the damage bonus. (In particular, [[whirlwind attack]] functions normally while in this combat mode.) * On a [[critical hit]] the bonus is multiplied after the roll (e.g. 2&times;(1d4) instead of 2d4 when the critical multiplier is x2). * This combat mode cannot be used with a [[ranged weapon]]. * Early in its development, this feat was going to be automatic instead of a combat mode.<sup>[http://nwn.bioware.com/shadows/faq.html#1.13]</sup>

{{feat |type=class |prereq=[[red dragon disciple]] |desc=The character becomes more draconic in appearance. His skin develops tiny iridescent scales, nearly invisible. This provides increasing natural armor bonuses to his base [[armor class]]. {{{!}}class="wikitable" style="text-align:center" {{!}}- ! class level {{!}} 1 {{!}}{{!}} 5 {{!}}{{!}} 8 {{!}}{{!}} 10 {{!}} 15 {{!}}{{!}} 20 {{!}}{{!}} 25 {{!}}{{!}} 30 {{!}}- ! AC bonus {{!}} +1 {{!}}{{!}} +2 {{!}}{{!}} +3 {{!}}{{!}} +4 {{!}} +5 {{!}}{{!}} +6 {{!}}{{!}} +7 {{!}}{{!}} +8 {{!}}} |use=automatic |icon=ife_x2ddarmor.gif |class1=red dragon disciple }}
==Notes== *Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. *The bonus is described as a "natural armor bonus", but it is actually an "[[armor class#Other|other bonus]]", which [[stack]]s with true [[Armor class#Natural bonus|natural bonuses]] to armor class.
==Custom content notes== * While this feat can be given to another class, the armor bonus is always based on levels in red dragon disciple.

{{feat |type=class |prereq=[[red dragon disciple]] 2 |desc=As the dragon disciple gains [[class level|level]]s in this [[prestige class]], his [[ability]] scores increase by the following table: {{{!}}border=0 style="margin:-2ex 2em 0ex" {{!}}- {{!}} Level {{!}}{{!}}&nbsp; {{!}}- {{!}} 2: {{!}}{{!}} +2 to [[strength]] {{!}}- {{!}} 4: {{!}}{{!}} +2 to strength {{!}}- {{!}} 7: {{!}}{{!}} +2 to [[constitution]] {{!}}- {{!}} 9: {{!}}{{!}} +2 to [[intelligence]] {{!}}- {{!}}10: {{!}}{{!}} +4 to strength, +2 to [[charisma]] {{!}}} |use=automatic |icon=ife x2ddarmor.gif |class1=red dragon disciple }}
==Notes== *Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. *The increase to Intelligence ''does'' apply increased skill point gain for the 9th level of Red Dragon Disciple, which if taken as soon as possible (14th Character Level) results in 27 extra skill points as of character level 40.
==Custom content notes== * While this feat can be given to another class, the ability increases depend upon levels in red dragon disciple. * If this feat is denied to red dragon disciples at level 2, the ability increases will be granted retroactively if this feat is obtained later. * If this feat is not acquired ''before'' taking a ninth level in red dragon disciple, the character will not be given wings.

{{feat |type=class |prereq=[[ranger]] 1 |desc=Rangers, when wearing [[light armor]], get all the benefits of having the [[ambidexterity]] and [[two-weapon fighting]] feats. While wearing [[medium armor|medium]] or [[heavy armor]] they lose these benefits. |use=automatic |icon=ife ambidex.gif |class1=ranger }}
==Notes==
* This feat does not qualify a character to take [[improved two-weapon fighting]] as a [[general feat]] selection. However, if nine levels of ranger are taken, ''improved two-weapon fighting'' will be granted automatically. * Wearing robes or no armor qualifies as "wearing light armor" for the purposes of this feat. * This feat serves only to inform the player; the benefits are hardcoded to the ranger class.

{{feat |epic=yes |type=class |prereq=[[barbarian]] 23 |desc=An epic barbarian's [[damage reduction]] allows him to ignore the first 5 points of damage from any physical attack. This ability increases by +1 point every 3rd [[class level|level]] past 23rd. |use=automatic |icon=ife_damred.gif |class1=barbarian }}
==Notes== *Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. *This feat replaces (does not [[stack]] with) the barbarian's pre-epic [[damage reduction (barbarian)|damage reduction]].
