{| border= 0 cellpadding=2 !width=50| !width=50| !width=50| !width=50| !width=50| !width=50| !width=50| |- |[[Image:Ife x2epskfanem.gif|right|Epic skill focus (animal empathy)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfappr.gif|right|Epic skill focus (appraise)]] |[[Image:Ife x2esfbluf.gif |right|Epic skill focus (bluff)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfconc.gif|right|Epic skill focus (concentration)]] |[[Image:Ife x2esfcrar.gif |right|Epic skill focus (craft armor)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfcrtr.gif|right|Epic skill focus (craft trap)]] |[[Image:Ife x2esfcrwp.gif |right|Epic skill focus (craft weapon)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2epskfdstr.gif|right|Epic skill focus (disable trap)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfdisc.gif|right|Epic skill focus (discipline)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfheal.gif|right|Epic skill focus (heal)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfhide.gif|right|Epic skill focus (hide)]] |[[Image:Ife x2esfinti.gif |right|Epic skill focus (intimidate)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskflist.gif|right|Epic skill focus (listen)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskflore.gif|right|Epic skill focus (lore)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2epskfmosi.gif|right|Epic skill focus (move silently)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfoplo.gif|right|Epic skill focus (open lock)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfparr.gif|right|Epic skill focus (parry)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfperf.gif|right|Epic skill focus (perform)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfpers.gif|right|Epic skill focus (persuade)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfpkpt.gif|right|Epic skill focus (pick pocket)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfsear.gif|right|Epic skill focus (search)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2epskfsttr.gif|right|Epic skill focus (set trap)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfspcr.gif|right|Epic skill focus (spellcraft)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfspot.gif|right|Epic skill focus (spot)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskftaun.gif|right|Epic skill focus (taunt)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskftumb.gif|right|Epic skill focus (tumble)]] |[[Image:Ife x2epskfusde.gif|right|Epic skill focus (use magic device)]] |} {{feat |epic=yes |type=general |prereq=21st level, 20 [[skill rank|rank]]s in the chosen skill |desc=The character gains a +10 bonus on all [[skill check]]s with the chosen [[skill]]. |use=automatic |bonus1=assassin |bonus2=bard |bonus3=Harper scout |bonus4=rogue |bonus5=shadowdancer }}
==Notes== *Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. *This feat [[stack]]s with [[skill focus]]. *There is no ''epic skill focus'' in [[ride]]. *''Epic skill focus'' in [[animal empathy]] can only be taken when gaining a [[druid]], [[ranger]], or [[shifter]] level; in [[perform]] only when gaining a [[bard]] level; in [[use magic device]] only when gaining a [[bard]], [[rogue]], or [[shadowdancer]] level. This would match the class restrictions on those skills if "shadowdancer" was replaced by "[[assassin]]". * ''Epic skill focus'' in ''use magic device'' cannot be selected as a rogue [[bonus feat]], but otherwise bonus feat availability matches [[general feat]] availability.
==Custom content notes== *A custom class must have three variants of this feat in their feat list, or that class will not be able to select those variants as [[general feat]]s. The three variants are ''epic skill focus'' in [[animal empathy]], [[perform]], and [[use magic device]] (i.e. the skills that are exclusive to certain classes). [[category:feats restricted by class, epic]]

{{feat |epic=yes |type=class |prereq=[[weapon of choice]], [[epic class|epic]] [[weapon master]] |desc=The weapon master gains a +1 bonus to all [[attack roll]]s with his weapon of choice at 13th level and every 3 levels afterwards. This bonus [[stack]]s with the weapon master's [[superior weapon focus]] feat. |use=automatic |icon=ife_x2supwpfo.gif |class1=weapon master }}
==Notes== *Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
{|class="wikitable" style="text-align:center" |- ! class level !! bonus |- | 13 || +1 |- | 16 || +2 |- | 19 || +3 |- | 22 || +4 |- | 25 || +5 |- | 28 || +6 |}

{{feat |epic=yes |type=general |prereq=21st level |desc=The character gains 20 [[hit point]]s. This feat may be taken multiple times, up to a maximum of 200 hit points. |use=automatic |icon=ife_x2tough1.gif |bonus1=arcane archer |bonus2=barbarian |bonus3=blackguard |bonus4=champion of Torm |bonus5=dwarven defender |bonus6=fighter |bonus7=monk |bonus8=paladin |bonus9=ranger |bonus10=red dragon disciple |bonus11=weapon master }}
==Notes==
*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. * Given the choice between this feat and [[great constitution]], the latter is usually the better choice. Taking ''epic toughness'' twice grants 40 hit points (regardless of level), while taking ''great constitution'' twice grants (indirectly) a +1 bonus to [[fortitude]] [[saving throw]]s and [[concentration]], in addition to (at level 40) granting 40 hit points. ** A notable exception is that this feat is usually the better choice for characters who typically [[polymorph]] into forms that override [[constitution]].

{| border=0 cellspacing=2 |- |[[Image:Ife x2wfbswd.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (bastard sword)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfbaxe.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (battleaxe)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfclub.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (club)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfcrea.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (creature weapon)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfdagg.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (dagger)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfdart.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (dart)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfdmac.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (dire mace)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfdaxe.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (double axe)]] |[[Image:Ife x2ewfdwax.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (dwarven waraxe)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2wfgaxe.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (greataxe)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfgswd.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (greatsword)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfhalb.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (halberd)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfhaxe.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (handaxe)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfhxb.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (heavy crossbow)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfhfla.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (heavy flail)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfkama.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (kama)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfkatn.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (katana)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfkukr.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (kukri)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2wflxb.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (light crossbow)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wflfla.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (light flail)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wflham.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (light hammer)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wflbow.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (longbow)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wflswd.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (longsword)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfmace.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (mace)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfmsta.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (morningstar)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfqsta.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (quarterstaff)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfrapr.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (rapier)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2wfscim.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (scimitar)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfscyt.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (scythe)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfsbow.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (shortbow)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfsswd.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (shortsword)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfshur.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (shuriken)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfskle.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (sickle)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfslng.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (sling)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfspr.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (spear)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wftaxe.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (throwing axe)]] |- |[[Image:Ife x2ewftri.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (trident)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wftswd.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (two-bladed sword)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfunar.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (unarmed strike)]] |[[Image:Ife x2wfwham.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (warhammer)]] |[[Image:Ife x2ewfwhip.gif|right|Epic weapon focus (whip)]] |} {{feat |epic=yes |type=combat |prereq=21st level, [[weapon focus]] with the chosen weapon |reqfor=[[epic weapon specialization]] |desc=The character gains a +2 bonus to all [[attack roll]]s with the chosen weapon. |use=automatic |bonus1=arcane archer |bonus2=barbarian |bonus3=blackguard |bonus4=champion of Torm |bonus5=dwarven defender |bonus6=fighter |bonus7=paladin |bonus8=ranger |bonus9=weapon master }}
==Notes== *Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. *[[Stack]]s with [[weapon focus]].
===Previous versions=== *Prior to version 1.69, ''epic weapon focus'' in the [[club]] had [[improved critical]] as the prerequisite instead of ''weapon focus''.

{{feat |type=general |prereq=[[intelligence]] 13+ |reqfor=[[improved expertise]], [[whirlwind attack]], [[improved whirlwind attack]], [[weapon master]] |desc=A character with this feat can make defensive attacks, gaining a +5 bonus to [[armor class|AC]] but receiving a -5 penalty to [[attack roll]]s. |use=combat mode |icon=ife_x1expert.gif |bonus1=champion of Torm |bonus2=fighter }}
==Notes==
*Added in the [[expansion pack]]s. *By default, NWN allows spellcasting while using ''expertise''. However, [[BioWare]] included a switch to disable it via scripting using [[spellhook]]ing. **Under the default behavior, this can be a useful feat for casters who do not make attacks, as they will gain the AC benefit at effectively no cost. *This is an often overlooked feat, but it can be incredibly useful to fighters facing very damaging enemies (or several annoying enemies). *This combat mode cannot be used while wielding a [[ranged weapon]].

{{feat |epic=yes |type=general |prereq=21st level, [[charisma]] 25+, either [[smite good]] or [[smite evil]] |desc=Whenever the character makes a successful smite attack, it adds two times the character's level to damage. This feat may be taken multiple times, up to a maximum of 10 times &mdash; each time adding additional damage equal to the character's level to the smite attack. |use=<del>combat mode</del> ''automatic'' |icon=ife_x2grsmt1.gif |bonus1=blackguard |bonus2=champion of Torm |bonus3=paladin }}
==Notes== *Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. *This feat was not described in the original Hordes of the Underdark manual. *This feat's description says "character level", but it is in fact the sum of [[champion of Torm]] and [[paladin]] [[class level]]s that is used for ''smite evil'', and [[blackguard]] class level for ''smite good''. *As an example, consider a character with 30 paladin and 10 champion of Torm levels. ''Smite evil'' by itself adds 40 damage to a successful smite. For each ''great smiting'' taken, an additional 40 damage is dealt. So if this character had ''great smiting I'', but not ''great smiting II'', a successful smite would deal a total of 80 extra damage. If this character had ''great smiting X'', a successful smite would deal a total of 440 extra damage.
==Custom content notes== *A custom class must have this feat in their feat list, or that class will not be able to select it as a general feat. [[category:feats restricted by class, epic]]

{{feat |epic=yes |type=general |prereq=21st level |desc=The character gains +1 to their [[strength]]. This may be taken multiple times, to a maximum bonus of +10. |use=automatic |icon=ife_x2grstr1.gif }}
==Notes==
*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. *Effectively, this feat can only be taken seven times, as there are only seven epic general feats, and no class has this as a [[bonus feat]].

{{feat |type=general |prereq=[[spell focus]] (selected [[spell school]]) |reqfor=[[epic spell focus]] |desc=A character becomes even more adept with spells of a particular [[spell school|school of magic]]. The character gains a +4 bonus to the spell save [[DC]] for all spells of the chosen school. |use=automatic. This feat may be selected multiple times, but the effects do not [[stack]]. It applies to a different school of magic in each case. |icon=ife_x1gsfabj.gif |bonus1=bard |bonus2=cleric |bonus3=druid |bonus4=paladin |bonus5=ranger |bonus6=red dragon disciple |bonus7=wizard }}
==Notes==
*Added in the [[expansion pack]]s. * ''Greater spell focus'' does not apply to spells that are granted as special abilities. * ''Greater spell focus'' does not stack with [[spell focus]]; it replaces the previous feat's benefits.

{{feat |type=class |prereq=[[red dragon disciple]] 4 |desc=As the dragon disciple gains levels in this [[prestige class]], his base [[hit die]] type changes. This change is not retroactive. {{{!}} class="wikitable" style="text-align:center" {{!}}- ! Level {{!}} 1 {{!!}} 4 {{!!}} 6 {{!!}} 11 {{!}}- ! Hit die {{!}} d6 {{!!}} d8 {{!!}} d10 {{!!}} d12 {{!}}} |use=automatic |icon=ife_ddhdincrease.gif |class1=red dragon disciple }}
==Notes== *Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
==Custom content notes== * While this feat can be given to another class, it only affects the hit points gained when taking a level in red dragon disciple.

{{feat |type=general |reqfor=[[superior initiative]] |desc=The character gains a +4 bonus to [[initiative]] checks. |use=automatic |icon=ife_x1init.gif }}
==Notes==
*Added in the [[expansion pack]]s.

{{feat |type=class |prereq=[[weapon of choice]], [[weapon master]] 5 |desc=With their weapon of choice, the [[critical multiplier|multiplier]] is increased by x1 to all [[critical hit]]s. Thus a x2 critical multiplier becomes a x3. |use=automatic |icon=ife_x2incmulti.gif |class1=weapon master }}
==Notes==
*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].

{{feat |type=class |prereq=[[weapon of choice]], [[weapon master]] 1 |desc=Once per day per [[class level|level]], a weapon master may use this feat to do maximum damage to their opponent. |use=selected |icon=ife_x2kidamage.gif |class=weapon master }}
==Notes==
*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]]. * This feat can be used only with a weapon of choice. *Using this feat does not guarantee a hit. This has some strategic consequences. **It is usually best to activate this feat for the first attack of a round (or any attack that is made at full [[base attack bonus]]). **It may be inefficient to activate this feat against a target that has high [[armor class]] or [[concealment]]. *Only the base weapon damage is maximized by this feat. If the weapon deals additional variable damage, it is possible that a ''ki damage'' hit will do less than the maximum possible total damage. A ''ki damage'' hit will still do more total damage on average than other hits. **On a critical hit ki damage will only maximize one instance of the base damage. Thus a mace with increased multiplier will deal 6 + 2d6 base weapon damage on a ki damage critical hit (as opposed to 3d6 without ki damage). *This is probably a bug, but [[epic dodge]] will activate vs. ''ki damage'' misses so this feat can be used to force an opponent with epic dodge to waste their dodge on a miss.

{{feat |type=general |prereq=Can only take this at first level. |desc=The character gains a +1 bonus on all [[saving throw]]s. |use=automatic |icon=ife_x1hero.gif }}
==Notes== *Added in the [[expansion pack]]s.
[[category:first level feats]]

{{feat |type=monster |prereq=none |desc=Using nonvisual senses, such as sensitivity to vibrations, scent, acute hearing, or echolocation, the creature maneuvers and fights as well as a sighted creature. [[Invisibility]] and [[darkness]] are irrelevant. The creature usually does not need to make [[spot]] or [[listen]] checks to notice creatures within the range of its blindsight ability (60 feet). |use=automatic |icon=ife_x2blindsigh.gif }}
== Notes ==
* This feat is only available for [[non-player character|NPCs]] by default.
